{"orgCode":"7900","name":"Public Employees' Retirement System","agencyCode":"7500","agencyName":"Government Operations","description":"The California Public Employees' Retirement System (CalPERS) administers retirement benefits for about 2,385,000 active employees and retirees of state and local agencies in California as of June 30, 2025. Benefits include retirement, disability, and survivor retirement benefits.\n\nCalPERS provides health benefits for approximately 1,568,000 active and retired state, local government, and school employees and their family members as of June 30, 2025. CalPERS develops, negotiates, and administers contracts with health maintenance organizations, group hospitals, and medical insurance plans. In addition, CalPERS administers a long-term care program for members and eligible individuals.\n\nCalPERS is governed by a Board of Administration. The California Constitution provides that the CalPERS Board of Administration has authority over the administration of the retirement system with the exception of the Health Benefits Program and Social Security.","website":"https://www.calpers.ca.gov","totals":{"amounts":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000},"positions":{"py":2464.6,"cy":2846.1,"by":2846.1},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":12417,"cy":15292,"by":14852},"nongovernmental":{"py":41580051,"cy":45402934,"by":49091135}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/7500/7900","kind":"department","name":"Public Employees' Retirement System","code":"7900","amounts":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000},"positions":{"py":2464.6,"cy":2846.1,"by":2846.1},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000}},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/9990","kind":"program","name":"Unscheduled Items of Appropriation","code":"9990","amounts":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/9990/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":337000,"cy":956000,"by":3018000}}}}]}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/7900","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/7900"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/7500/7900.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY\n\nGovernment Code, Title 2, Division 5, Parts 3, 4, and 5; and California Constitution, Article XVI, Section 17."},"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410","kind":"program","name":"Retirement","code":"6410","amounts":{"py":117236,"cy":125891,"by":131742},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":117236,"cy":125891,"by":131742}},"positions":{"py":654.4,"cy":765.7,"by":765.7},"description":"6410 - RETIREMENT\n\nCalPERS provides retirement planning education, service and disability retirement, refunds, and survivor and death benefits for employees of California public employers. CalPERS provides special benefits based on death or disability incurred in the line of duty for members in certain occupations. As of June 30, 2025, there were about 1,560,000 active and inactive members, and about 825,000 retirees, survivors, and beneficiaries under the CalPERS system.\n\nBasic retirement benefits are generally based upon three factors: age at retirement, years of service, and final compensation. There are different formulas for each of the member categories, such as Miscellaneous, Industrial, Peace Officer/Firefighter, California Highway Patrol, and Safety. Over 50 contract options are available to local cities, counties, and districts that contract with CalPERS. However, state and local employees hired after January 1, 2013 will generally be limited to one of five benefit formulas. A member's retirement and death benefits are determined by statute and/or contract provisions.\n\nAs of June 30, 2025, there were 2,906 public agency and school district employers providing CalPERS retirement, death, and survivor benefits to California public employees. CalPERS benefits may be transferable for members who continue their careers with many other public employers in California as a result of agreements between CalPERS and other public agency retirement systems.\n\nCalPERS also administers the Legislators' and Judges' Retirement Systems.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":117236,"cy":125891,"by":131742}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0815","kind":"fund","name":"Judges Retirement Fund","code":"0815","amounts":{"py":2059,"cy":2275,"by":2129},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":2059,"cy":2275,"by":2129}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2059,"cy":2275,"by":2129}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0820","kind":"fund","name":"Legislators Retirement Fund","code":"0820","amounts":{"py":652,"cy":704,"by":715},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":652,"cy":704,"by":715}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":652,"cy":704,"by":715}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0830","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Retirement Fund","code":"0830","amounts":{"py":103444,"cy":109996,"by":115820},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":103444,"cy":109996,"by":115820}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":103444,"cy":109996,"by":115820}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0833","kind":"fund","name":"Annuitants Health Care Coverage Fund","code":"0833","amounts":{"py":7568,"cy":8890,"by":8760},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":7568,"cy":8890,"by":8760}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":7568,"cy":8890,"by":8760}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0849","kind":"fund","name":"Replacement Benefit Custodial Fund","code":"0849","amounts":{"py":550,"cy":625,"by":691},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":550,"cy":625,"by":691}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":550,"cy":625,"by":691}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f0884","kind":"fund","name":"Judges Retirement System II Fund","code":"0884","amounts":{"py":2708,"cy":3092,"by":3294},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":2708,"cy":3092,"by":3294}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2708,"cy":3092,"by":3294}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6410/f9251","kind":"fund","name":"California Employers' Pension Prefunding Trust Fund","code":"9251","amounts":{"py":255,"cy":309,"by":333},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":255,"cy":309,"by":333}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":255,"cy":309,"by":333}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6412","kind":"program","name":"Social Security","code":"6412","amounts":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162}},"positions":{"py":5,"cy":5,"by":5},"description":"6412 - SOCIAL SECURITY\n\nCalPERS serves as California's designated State Social Security Administrator (SSSA) and oversees agreements between the federal government and public employers who provide Social Security benefits to their employees under the Old-Age, Survivors, Disability, and Health Insurance provisions of the federal Social Security Act. As the SSSA, CalPERS acts as the liaison between the Social Security Administration and approximately 2,300 public agencies. The program is responsible for administering new coverage agreements, processing coverage modifications, providing education to employers, and collecting and reporting information to the Social Security Administration.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6412/f0652","kind":"fund","name":"Old Age and Survivors Insurance Revolving Fund","code":"0652","amounts":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":858,"cy":1161,"by":1162}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6415","kind":"program","name":"Health Benefits","code":"6415","amounts":{"py":72017,"cy":87832,"by":87947},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":72017,"cy":87832,"by":87947}},"positions":{"py":247,"cy":247,"by":247},"description":"6415 - HEALTH BENEFITS\n\nThe Health Benefits Branch program contracts with health maintenance organizations, claim administrators, employee associations, and others to provide health insurance for state, California State University, and local public agency employees, retirees, and their dependents. The program negotiates and monitors health plan contracts, develops cost-effective programs, provides enrollment services to members and employers, and meets and confers with employee organizations and employer representatives.\n\nAdditionally, this program maintains demographic and statistical information systems; establishes standards for Basic, Supplement to Medicare, and Managed Medicare health plans; establishes and maintains health benefits coverage for all eligible employees and retirees; provides accurate and timely accounting for participating agencies; and serves as an impartial intermediary between CalPERS enrollees and insurance carriers in resolving claim and service disputes.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":72017,"cy":87832,"by":87947}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6415/f0822","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Health Care Fund (PEHCF)","code":"0822","amounts":{"py":39672,"cy":51830,"by":51894},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":39672,"cy":51830,"by":51894}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":39672,"cy":51830,"by":51894}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6415/f0950","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Contingency Reserve Fund","code":"0950","amounts":{"py":32345,"cy":36002,"by":36053},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":32345,"cy":36002,"by":36053}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":32345,"cy":36002,"by":36053}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6420","kind":"program","name":"Investment Operations","code":"6420","amounts":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539}},"positions":{"py":309.9,"cy":371,"by":371},"description":"6420 - INVESTMENT OPERATIONS\n\nThrough this program, CalPERS invests funds in various investment categories (stocks, bonds, real estate, etc.) for the purpose of minimizing the employers' contributions to the system needed to provide benefits to active participants, retired members, and their beneficiaries. Since CalPERS was established in 1932, investment assets of the Public Employees' Retirement Fund have grown from $800,000 to a total of $563.0 billion, as of June 30, 2025.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6420/f0830","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Retirement Fund","code":"0830","amounts":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":108295,"cy":142715,"by":148539}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6425","kind":"program","name":"Administration","code":"6425","amounts":{"py":224291,"cy":257279,"by":268488},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":12417,"cy":15292,"by":14852},"nongovernmental":{"py":211874,"cy":241987,"by":253636}},"positions":{"py":1248.3,"cy":1457.4,"by":1457.4},"description":"6425 - ADMINISTRATION\n\nThis program provides executive direction, specialized information, and administrative support necessary to administer all of the CalPERS programs. The various services include: Audits, Diversity Outreach, Enterprise Compliance, Enterprise Strategy Performance, Executive, Financial Office, Human Resources, Information Technology, Legal, Legislative Affairs, Long Term Care, Operational Support, and Public Affairs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":224291,"cy":257279,"by":268488}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6425/f0830","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Retirement Fund","code":"0830","amounts":{"py":211874,"cy":241987,"by":253636},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":211874,"cy":241987,"by":253636}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":211874,"cy":241987,"by":253636}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6425/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":12417,"cy":15292,"by":14852},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":12417,"cy":15292,"by":14852}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":12417,"cy":15292,"by":14852}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6430","kind":"program","name":"Benefit Payments","code":"6430","amounts":{"py":41069771,"cy":44803348,"by":48468109},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":41069771,"cy":44803348,"by":48468109}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Unclassified":{"py":41069771,"cy":44803348,"by":48468109}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6430/f0822","kind":"fund","name":"Public Employees Health Care Fund (PEHCF)","code":"0822","amounts":{"py":4783956,"cy":5596340,"by":6270064},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":4783956,"cy":5596340,"by":6270064}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"Unclassified":{"py":4783956,"cy":5596340,"by":6270064}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7900/6430/f0830","k